ve operations. 6.1 Shared-ground join For two positive factors and no join insertion, r = 1+(a-1)+(b-1) = a+b-1. Hence  oxed{g(a,b)=a+b-1.} The subtraction is the shared ground occupation. A sector-coordinate source of real depth d carries the relative level d-1. Joining it to mode n therefore gives  oxed{g(d,n)=d+n-1.} The electroweak chain becomes n_W = 1+(72-1)+(5-1) =76, n_Z = 1+(76-1)+(6-1) =81, and n_H = 1+(15-1)+(81-1) =95. 6.2 Antisymmetric binary join For two positive factors and one degree-one join insertion, r = 1+(a-1)+(b-1)+1 = a+b. Therefore  oxed{r=a+b.} The charged-lepton and strange/tau relations are n_s = 1+(3-1)+(1-1)+1 =4, n_e = 1+(10-1)+(3-1)+1 =13, n_\mu = 1+(15-1)+(20-1)+1 =35, and n_	au = 1+(22-1)+(1-1)+1 =23. The extra unit is interpreted as one phase quantum carried by the antisymmetric pairing node. 6.3 Inclusion--exclusion source For two positive factors and one conjugated shared factor, r = 1+(a-1)+(b-1)-(c-1) = a+b-c. Thus  oxed{r=a+b-c.} The third neutrino index follows from the cubic source \psi_{
