oes not produce a global tangent splitting: Section 15.1a proves that the literal complex tangent bundle of Q_{10}=\mathbb{CP}^5 admits no rank-3+2 splitting at all. A different globally admissible carrier and its dynamical selection law are required. The unitary stabilizer of the split is U(3)	imes U(2). Its intersection with SU(5), after separately imposing determinant one, is S(U(3)	imes U(2)) = \left\{ (g_c,g_w): \det g_c\det g_w=1 ight\}. Its global group form is S(U(3)	imes U(2)) \cong  rac{SU(3)	imes SU(2)	imes U(1)}{\mathbb Z_6}. A central generator commuting with SU(3)	imes SU(2) has the form Y=y_cI_3\oplus y_wI_2. The determinant condition gives 3y_c+2y_w=0. Minimal conventional normalization fixes, up to overall sign,  oxed{ Y=- rac13I_3\oplus rac12I_2. } 13. One chiral depth-ten fibre contains one family representation Decompose the positive-chirality spinor as S_{10}^+ = \Lambda^{m even}(V_c\oplus V_w). Then S_{10}^+ =  igoplus_{\substack{0\leq p\leq3\0\leq q\leq2\p+q\ {m even}}} \Lambda^pV_c\otimes\Lambda^qV_w. On the (p,q) component, the Abelian generator acts with weight  oxed{ Y(p,q)=- rac p3+ rac q2. } The complete branching is (p,q) SU(3)	imes SU(2) representation Y left-handed-field interpretation (0,0) (\mathbf1,\mathbf1) 0 
